The fork renames the product, replaces its CI, logos and documentation,
trims the default feature set, and adds the `init` template writer, the
cross-platform release pipeline and the client onboarding guide.

It links against these third-party crates, each under its own license:

  pimalaya-cli, pimalaya-config, pimalaya-stream   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  io-imap, io-smtp, io-sasl, io-maildir, io-mbox   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  io-jmap, io-gmail, io-msgraph, io-pimdir         MIT OR Apache-2.0
  io-http, ical-rs, mime-rs                        MIT OR Apache-2.0
  serde, serde_json, clap, anyhow, chrono, toml    MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rusqlite (bundled SQLite)                        MIT
  ring, rustls                                     Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  schemars, secrecy, log, url, base64              MIT OR Apache-2.0

The full list with versions is in Cargo.lock; the license texts shipped
inside each dependency are the authoritative terms. SQLite is vendored
from source (the `vendored` feature).
